WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.456
A fixed-width bit pattern has meaning only under an interpretation.

00:00:05.456 --> 00:00:09.275
In eight-bit unsigned form, 11111111 represents 255.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:13.094
In eight-bit two’s complement, it represents −1.

00:00:13.094 --> 00:00:19.095
The representable range for n-bit two’s complement is −2^(n−1) through 2^(n−1)−1.

00:00:20.095 --> 00:00:21.651
+5 is 00000101.

00:00:21.651 --> 00:00:25.282
Inversion gives 11111010; adding one gives 11111011.

00:00:25.282 --> 00:00:38.250
The high bit has weight −128, so the value is −128 + 64 + 32 + 16 + 8 + 2 + 1 = −5.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.246
What is the eight-bit signed range?

00:00:42.246 --> 00:00:47.240
Eight-bit two’s complement has 256 values, from −128 to 127.
